# Keep api/'s TOP-LEVEL test files out of the Vercel deployment bundle.
#
# Vercel turns every top-level file in api/ into a serverless function. A test
# file like api/payments.test.js would therefore be deployed as a function,
# consuming a slot against the Hobby-plan limit of 12 (we are already at 12) and
# potentially failing the build. Excluding them here means they are never
# uploaded, so they can never be mistaken for functions.
#
# Scoped to api/*.test.* (top level only), NOT api/**/*.test.* (all depths):
# Vercel's own zero-config API detection already ignores underscore-prefixed
# directories like api/_lib/ (see scripts/lint-api-functions.js's own doc
# comment) — those test files were never at risk, and excluding them anyway
# strips them from the vercel-build container, so `npm run test` silently ran
# a smaller suite there than in CI (18/33 files, missing the payments/auth/
# credit suites under api/_lib/). Only the 5 top-level api/*.test.* files pose
# the actual function-count risk.
api/*.test.js
api/*.test.ts
api/*.spec.js
api/*.spec.ts
